// =============================================================================
// xos2.xl - Complete Operating System Simulator
// =============================================================================
// A from-scratch, single-file OS simulator written in xlang.
//
// Subsystems modelled:
//   1. Boot loader        - POST + kernel bring-up + init (PID 1)
//   2. Process manager    - PCB, MLFQ scheduler (Q0=2/Q1=4/Q2=8), boost,
//                           fork / exec / wait / exit, signal delivery
//   3. Memory manager     - two-level page tables, 64-entry LRU TLB,
//                           swappable page replacement (LRU / CLOCK / OPT),
//                           shared memory (SHM), copy-on-write fork
//   4. File system        - inode FS with hardlinks and symbolic links,
//                           VFS with mount points, rwx permissions,
//                           per-process fd tables, anonymous pipes + FIFOs,
//                           device files (/dev/null, /dev/zero, /dev/random,
//                           /dev/console)
//   5. Shell              - pipeline / redirect / background / sequence,
//                           environment variables (PATH, HOME, PWD, USER),
//                           built-in commands and command history
//   6. Syscall interface  - unified syscall(op, args) dispatcher
//
// CLI:
//   xos2 boot <script.xsh>   boot the kernel and execute a shell script
//   xos2 test                run the integrated self-test suite
//   xos2 help                show usage
//
// All comments are pure ASCII on purpose: xlang's lexer honours // and the
// file is parsed as UTF-8, which keeps the source portable across locales.
//
// xlang notes baked into this implementation:
//   * derive value classes are stored in typed arrays; mutation requires a
//     read -> modify -> write-back cycle (g_arr[i].field = v then write back).
//   * Return type uses 'as', not '->'. while loops require 'do'.
//   * No stdin API: scripts are loaded with file.readText and parsed.
//   * auto cannot infer pop() return, so explicit types are used everywhere.
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
//  Part 0: Constants
// =============================================================================

